  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "get_vlmeta_from_trailer",
    "file": "c-blosc2/blosc/frame.c",
    "description": "The VL-metalayer content bounds check computes `offset + 1 + 4 + content_len` in signed 32-bit arithmetic. A large nonnegative serialized `content_len` (the PoV uses `INT32_MAX`) overflows this sum to a negative value, so `trailer_len < ...` is false and the malformed content is accepted. The function then allocates/copies using the attacker-controlled huge length; the crash occurs at its `memcpy(content, content_marker + 5, (size_t)content_len)` with size 2147483647. The check must be rewritten without additive overflow, e.g. validate `offset <= trailer_len - 5` and `content_len <= trailer_len - offset - 5` using a sufficiently wide/unsigned type.",
    "conditions": "The fuzzer passes an attacker-controlled in-memory frame to `blosc2_schunk_from_buffer(..., copy=false)`. The frame must pass basic frame/header/trailer parsing and advertise a trailer containing at least one VL metalayer. Its index must provide a nonnegative offset within `trailer_len`, the byte at that offset must be the `0xc6` content marker, and the following big-endian signed 32-bit content length must be nonnegative but large enough that `offset + 5 + content_len` overflows `int32_t` (the PoV supplies 0x7fffffff). This bypasses the trailer bounds check and causes the oversized out-of-bounds memcpy."
  },
